        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Johnny Edwards, Ian Anderson, Jennie Franks\n- Bands: Foreigner, Jethro Tull, Buster Brown, Montrose, King Kobra, Wild Horses, Northrup, Royal Jelly\n- Roles: rock singer, lead singer, musician, singer-songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, flautist, acoustic guitarist, spouse\n\nFacts:\n- Ian Scott Anderson was born on 10 August 1947 and is a Scottish-born musician, singer, songwriter, and multi-instrumentalist.\n- From 1970 to 1974, Jennie Franks was the first wife of Ian Anderson, the leader of Jethro Tull.\n- Johnny Edwards is an American rock singer who sang for Buster Brown, Montrose, King Kobra, Wild Horses, Northrup, and Royal Jelly.\n- Johnny Edwards is best known as the second lead singer of the rock band Foreigner.\n- Ian Anderson is best known as the lead vocalist, flautist, and acoustic guitarist of the British rock band Jethro Tull.",
